add('c0770','abcwarriors-martian-work-zero','ABC Warriors (the Martian human-robot economy)','ABC Warriors','The functioning Martian settlement economy amid robot conflict','Living biological human Martian residents','Warrior robots’ real work is disclosed; a battle unit or farm is not a population employment statistic.',
'''War robots and conflict on Mars coexist with farms and useful human labor. Artificial combat and technical capacity therefore do not establish that ordinary human production has disappeared. The guarantee best guess is weak because continuing settlement access is vulnerable to conflict and hierarchy. This zero variant treats robotic substitution as a limited material comparison, without claiming that a robot army already supplies every household free food and care.

 Human institutions and powerful operators receive central control weight, qualified by autonomous robot agency. An independent warrior is not automatically the sovereign provider of the whole Martian economy. The low nonworking scenario counts farming, services, maintenance, administration, care and assigned defense. Robot contribution remains real work where the robots are persons, while the scoped percentage concerns living humans. The broad intervals preserve ordinary household uncertainty and period differences. The record does not turn warfare casualties or ruined farms into a population released from labor.''',
(.75,.15,.25),([-.4,.98],[-.85,.65],[.02,.85]),('Conflict and hierarchy make secure settlement access weak centrally.','Human institutions coexist with powerful autonomous robot actors.','Human farms and useful roles remain; robot work and casualties are not human leisure.'),
['War robots and later Martian conflict coexist with farms and human labor.'],['The ordinary robotic-substitution floor is a low-confidence interpretation.','Human and sentient robot work are separately disclosed.'],'Retain the familiar mixed-person working colony with its limited material qualification explicit.')

